<description>
Reflect the square grid across its uniform foreground main diagonal.

Input structure
- The input is a square grid with a dominant background color.
- The main diagonal is a complete one-color foreground line.
- The diagonal color appears only on that line; other foreground colors are off the line.

Rule
- Keep the diagonal fixed and move every off-diagonal pixel to the cell with swapped row/column coordinates.
- Equivalently, return the matrix transpose of the input grid.

Key insight
- The one-color diagonal is the reflection axis, so color values are preserved while coordinates are transposed.
</description>
<annotation>
{
  "type": "symmetry/pattern",
  "src": "square grid with a complete one-color main diagonal as the mirror axis",
  "transform": "transpose the grid across that diagonal: each cell at (r,c) moves to (c,r), preserving colors"
}
</annotation>
<generation_spec>
```yaml
spec:
  grid: square NxN, N in 3-6
  background: 0 (black)
  diagonal:
    color: 5 (gray), fills entire main diagonal (r==c)
    appears only on the diagonal (exactly N cells of this color)
  off_diagonal_pixels:
    location: strictly below the main diagonal (r > c); upper triangle is all background
    distinct_colors: 1-4, each different from bg and diagonal color
    cells_per_color: 1-2, forming an axis-aligned segment (horizontal or vertical)
    total_fg_cells: 1-7, density ~30-50% of lower triangle
    no_overlap: no two color groups share a cell; no cell at (r,c) AND (c,r) both non-bg [observed]
  transform: transpose the grid (swap rows and columns); diagonal stays fixed, lower-triangle pixels move to upper triangle

generation_strategy:
  approach: direct construction (task is simple enough)
  steps:
    1. Pick N uniformly from 3-6.
    2. Create NxN grid filled with bg=0; set diagonal to color 5.
    3. Pick k = randint(1, min(4, N-1)) distinct colors from palette minus {0, 5}.
    4. For each color, pick size 1 or 2. Place as a horizontal or vertical segment
       in the strict lower triangle (r > c), ensuring no overlap with existing fg cells.
    5. Verify total fg cells >= 1 and density <= 50% of lower-triangle cells.
    6. Return the grid as input; output = input.T.
```
</generation_spec>
