<description>
Continue the grey-bracketed top motif downward through the empty suffix.

Input structure
The grid has a black background. A contiguous run of grey pixels begins at
the top of the leftmost column; those grey pixels mark the rows of a colored
motif. Below the marked rows there may be other foreground rows, followed by
an all-background suffix.

Rule
Copy the marked rows as a motif after changing the grey marker cells to
background. Starting just below the lowest existing foreground row, write
those motif rows cyclically into the empty suffix, preserving the original
grid everywhere else.

Key insight
The grey segment is a bracket for the motif height; the fill below the
existing drawing restarts from the first marked row rather than continuing
from any unmarked foreground row.
</description>
<annotation>
{
  "summary": "Extend the grey-marked top motif downward through the empty bottom rows.",
  "type": "symmetry/pattern",
  "src": "top row motif marked by a contiguous grey run in the leftmost column, with the grey marker cells excluded",
  "dst": "empty suffix rows below the lowest existing foreground row",
  "transform": "repeat the marked motif rows cyclically from the first marked row into the suffix; preserve all existing pixels elsewhere"
}
</annotation>
<generation_spec>
```yaml
spec:
  grid: 5-13 rows x 5-7 cols, black background
  structure: |
    Three vertical zones stacked top-to-bottom:
    1. MARKER zone (rows 0..M-1): grey(5) in col 0, colored motif in cols 1+
    2. MIDDLE zone (M..M+K-1): non-grey foreground pixels, col 0 always black
    3. SUFFIX zone (M+K..H-1): entirely black (to be filled)
  marker:
    height: 1-4 rows (contiguous run of grey in col 0 starting at row 0)
    grey_pixels: exactly one per marker row (col 0 only); no grey elsewhere
    motif: each marker row has 1-3 non-bg pixels in cols 1+; 2-3 distinct colors total
    motif_width: bounding box spans 2-3 columns; leftmost motif col >= 1
  middle:
    height: 1-3 rows, all below marker zone
    content: 1-5 foreground pixels, uses 1-3 colors (may overlap motif colors or not)
    col_overlap_with_motif: columns overlap with motif region [observed]
  suffix:
    height: 2-8 rows, always >= marker height
    content: entirely black in input
  right_padding: 1-2 empty columns on the right [observed]
  output:
    input rows preserved; suffix filled with motif (grey replaced by black) repeated cyclically

generation_strategy:
  approach: direct construction (input structure is simple enough)
  steps:
    1. Pick H (5-13), W (5-7), M (1-4 marker rows), K (1-3 middle rows), ensure suffix = H-M-K >= max(2, M)
    2. Build motif rows (M rows): place 1-3 colored pixels per row in cols 1..W-2, using 2-3 non-grey/non-black colors; ensure bounding box width 2-3
    3. Set col 0 of marker rows to grey(5)
    4. Build middle rows (K rows): place 1-5 foreground pixels (non-grey, non-black) in cols 1..W-2, columns overlapping with motif region
    5. Leave suffix rows as black
    6. Build output by copying input, then filling suffix with motif (col 0 = black) cyclically
```
